course: dictionary
lesson: 6731
title: Okay: many meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: «Okay» is a small word with many meanings, so read the words around it to find the right one. «Are you okay?» means are you all right, not hurt or upset.
explain: «Is it okay if I go?» means is it allowed. «The film was okay.» means it was quite good but not very good. Ask: what would fit here? Then try your meaning in the sentence and see if it still makes sense.
explain: «Okay!» on its own means yes, I agree. «Okay, let's begin» uses okay to start a new topic. It is informal, so you will often hear it in speech and modern stories.
fact: Okay can be an adjective, an adverb, an exclamation or a verb, and it is also spelled OK.
fact: «Okay» means all right, fine, not hurt or not upset.
fact: «Okay» means acceptable or allowed.
fact: «Okay» can mean quite good but not very good, as in «the film was okay».
fact: It's okay to feel sad, angry or scared, and it's okay to say no.
exercise: Mia said «Okay, no worries» and didn't push. What does okay mean here? | Angry and loud | Wet and grey | *All right, no problem | Lost in the woods
exercise: Ella asks, «Is it okay if I go?» What is she asking? | *Is it allowed? | Is it very old? | Is it dangerous? | Is it short and rude?
exercise: «The film was okay.» What does okay suggest about the film? | Terrible and very loud | *Quite good but not very good | Excellent, the best ever | Very old
test: «Are you okay?» is the first question to ask someone who has fallen over. What does it mean? | Are you going home? | *Are you all right, or are you hurt? | Are you hungry? | Are you lost?
test: Which sentence is true? | *It's okay to feel sad, angry or scared | Feeling sad is not allowed | Only happy feelings are okay | Okay means silly
exam: In «Okay, let's begin», what job does okay do? | It means very old | It means dangerous | It means very hungry | *It starts a new topic
